  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301035-402</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Centre of Expertise on Illicit Finance (ODA eligible projects)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICE will enhance the FCDO country network and policy teams&#x2019; ability to deliver impact by providing the following functions: Horizon scanning into future IF risks and vulnerabilities across the international system. This will be disseminated through briefs and alerts. It will include analysis into future jurisdictions where IF may pose a threat to UK and developing countries&#x2019; interests: Specialist action-oriented research and analysis into IF systems and vulnerabilities related to specific geographies and themes. This will analyse a broad range of sources and data sets, and draw on expertise and information in think tanks, academia, and NGOs: Flexible advisory support to develop and strengthen technically sound and politically feasible IF responses and interventions to IF and sources of IF, drawing on deployable experts with deep sectoral expertise: Monitoring, evaluation, and lesson learning on &#x2018;what works&#x2019; to enhance resilience to IF across the international system: and a hub for knowledge, evidence, learning, and expert partnerships on IF.</narrative>
  </description>
